/-!
# The chart-extension final topology on compactly supported bundle sections

Compactly supported `C^n` sections of a real vector bundle `V → M` (`n : ℕ∞`) carry a canonical
cover-free locally convex topology `ContMDiffSection.chartTestTopology`: the final locally convex
topology (`TauCeti.finalLocallyConvexTopology`) generated by all native test-function extension
maps `Bundle.Trivialization.chartTestSection` over smooth charts subordinate to smooth bundle
trivializations (`ContMDiffSection.ChartTestDatum`).

By construction, a linear map (over `ℝ` or any `ℝ`-algebra) from compactly supported sections into
a locally convex real topological vector space is continuous for `chartTestTopology` if and only if
its composition with every native chart-extension map `t.chartTestSection c hc hct` is continuous
(`ContMDiffSection.continuous_chartTestTopology_iff`). Moreover, when the bundle also carries a
compatible structure over a normed `ℝ`-algebra `𝕜'` (in particular `𝕜' = ℂ`), constant `𝕜'`-scalar
multiplication is continuous for `chartTestTopology` without any manifold-regularity or
dimensionality hypothesis, and `𝕜'`-scalar multiplication is jointly continuous whenever `𝕜'` is
finite-dimensional over `ℝ` (`ContMDiffSection.continuousSMul_chartTestTopology_ofNormedAlgebra`).

In the converse direction, any chart `c` with `C^n` inverse subordinate to a smooth trivialization
`t` reads sections supported in a compact subset `K ⊆ c.source` continuously back into
`𝓓^{n}_{K'}(E, F)` and `𝓓^{n}(⟨c.target, c.open_target⟩, F)`
(`Bundle.Trivialization.chartReadSupportedIn`, `Bundle.Trivialization.chartReadTestFunction`), and
reads arbitrary sections localized by a compactly supported `C^n` cutoff `ρ` with
`tsupport ρ ⊆ c.source` continuously into `𝓓^{n}(⟨c.target, c.open_target⟩, F)`
(`Bundle.Trivialization.chartCutoffTestFunction`). When `c.source = univ`, extension by zero is a
continuous linear equivalence `𝓓^{n}(⟨c.target, c.open_target⟩, F) ≃L[ℝ] compactlySupported I F n V`
(`Bundle.Trivialization.chartTestSectionEquiv`).

When `E` is finite-dimensional and `M` is a Hausdorff `C^n` manifold covered by two-sided `C^n`
charts (in particular, on every boundaryless Hausdorff finite-dimensional `C^n` manifold), a finite
`C^n` partition of unity on each compact support identifies `chartTestTopology` with the
fixed-compact inductive-limit topology `ContMDiffSection.compactlySupportedTopology` of any
covering smooth frame system (`ContMDiffSection.chartTestTopology_eq_compactlySupportedTopology`),
and with the final locally convex topology of the preferred chart extensions at points of `M`
(`ContMDiffSection.chartTestTopology_eq_finalLocallyConvexTopology_preferredChartAt`).
-/

public noncomputable section

open Bundle Set TopologicalSpace Topology
